1
00:00:23,780 --> 00:00:25,320
Everyone, attack!

2
00:00:38,700 --> 00:00:39,940
Yeah!

3
00:00:41,080 --> 00:00:42,320
Yeah!

4
00:00:43,600 --> 00:00:44,720
Yeah! Yeah!

5
00:01:09,440 --> 00:01:12,960
I don't know.

6
00:01:30,520 --> 00:01:35,857
If you feel the same way, I
will be able to see the moon.

7
00:01:35,940 --> 00:01:40,637
And I will be able to see the moon.

8
00:01:40,720 --> 00:01:44,577
And I will be able to see the moon.

9
00:01:44,660 --> 00:01:49,817
As long as the body is.

10
00:01:49,900 --> 00:01:54,200
Don't miss one but I'm gonna leave it.

11
00:01:55,000 --> 00:01:57,337
I'm a small heart.

12
00:01:57,420 --> 00:01:59,620
I'm a big sinner.

13
00:02:01,160 --> 00:02:03,537
I'm a weak person.

14
00:02:03,620 --> 00:02:05,097
You can feel me.

15
00:02:05,180 --> 00:02:07,237
I'm a strong world.

16
00:02:07,320 --> 00:02:09,020
I'm a strong person.

17
00:02:11,120 --> 00:02:11,977
I'm a long life.

18
00:02:12,060 --> 00:02:13,297
I'm a heart.

19
00:02:13,380 --> 00:02:15,320
I'm so forever.

20
00:02:41,300 --> 00:02:42,980
How many did we lose?

21
00:02:49,720 --> 00:02:51,160
14 of us died.

22
00:02:52,200 --> 00:02:53,460
Oh my god!

23
00:02:56,100 --> 00:02:58,957
And we still got 25 floors to go.

24
00:02:59,040 --> 00:03:00,817
25 more floors.

25
00:03:00,900 --> 00:03:03,724
How the hell are we even
gonna make it that far?

26
00:03:27,920 --> 00:03:28,750
What's wrong?

27
00:03:41,900 --> 00:03:42,730
Kirito!

28
00:03:42,813 --> 00:03:43,643
What are you?

29
00:03:52,840 --> 00:03:54,300
An immortal object?

30
00:03:55,560 --> 00:03:57,960
Commander Heathcliff, what's going on?

31
00:03:58,500 --> 00:04:00,480
I think I got the answer to that.

32
00:04:01,020 --> 00:04:03,057
Reason why the Commander's HP never hits

33
00:04:03,140 --> 00:04:05,905
yellow is because he's
protected by the system.

34
00:04:07,360 --> 00:04:12,184
You know, ever since day one, something's
always bugged me about this whole thing.

35
00:04:12,680 --> 00:04:14,320
I was always wondering,

36
00:04:14,620 --> 00:04:18,917
where is he hiding while he watches us
and controls everything in this world?

37
00:04:19,000 --> 00:04:21,320
Well, the answer's pretty simple.

38
00:04:21,740 --> 00:04:23,400
It's basic psychology.

39
00:04:23,980 --> 00:04:27,240
In fact, it's so simple
every kid knows it.

40
00:04:27,580 --> 00:04:31,521
There's nothing more boring than
watching someone else play an RPG.

41
00:04:32,940 --> 00:04:35,440
Is there, Akihiko Kayaba?

42
00:04:39,000 --> 00:04:43,297
Just for my curiosity's sake, would you
mind telling me how you figured it out?

43
00:04:43,380 --> 00:04:46,851
The first time I knew something
was up was during our duel.

44
00:04:48,160 --> 00:04:50,317
Remember when you turned the tables on me?

45
00:04:50,400 --> 00:04:52,200
That move was way too fast.

46
00:04:53,060 --> 00:04:54,280
Yes, I thought so.

47
00:04:54,640 --> 00:04:57,617
It was a mistake to think that
would go unnoticed by you.

48
00:04:57,700 --> 00:04:59,820
But you were so strong and so fast,

49
00:04:59,940 --> 00:05:03,528
the only choice I had was to
engage the system's assist mode.

50
00:05:08,740 --> 00:05:11,000
Yes, I am Akihiko Kayaba.

51
00:05:11,280 --> 00:05:13,557
And now that my identity's been revealed,

52
00:05:13,640 --> 00:05:17,875
it should come as no surprise that I
am the final boss on the top floor.

53
00:05:20,700 --> 00:05:25,140
So the strongest player in the whole
game ends up being the final boss.

54
00:05:25,400 --> 00:05:26,871
Kind of cliche, isn't it?

55
00:05:27,180 --> 00:05:29,298
Actually, I kind of like that angle.

56
00:05:30,360 --> 00:05:31,497
One thing's for sure,

57
00:05:31,580 --> 00:05:34,657
I always thought you'd be the one
standing before me at the very end.

58
00:05:34,740 --> 00:05:37,200
You know, dual-wielding is a rare skill,

59
00:05:37,440 --> 00:05:40,957
the kind that's only given to the
player with the fastest reaction time.

60
00:05:41,040 --> 00:05:45,760
He is the hero of this story, the one
who rises up to challenge the Demon King.

61
00:05:46,220 --> 00:05:49,920
But you, the power you've
displayed exceeded my expectations.

62
00:05:50,480 --> 00:05:52,737
I guess these unexpected twists and turns

63
00:05:52,820 --> 00:05:56,260
are what makes MMORPG
so thrilling to play.

64
00:05:57,960 --> 00:06:00,540
Our loyalty, our hope.

65
00:06:00,820 --> 00:06:01,780
How dare you?

66
00:06:02,000 --> 00:06:02,837
How dare you?

67
00:06:02,920 --> 00:06:04,420
How dare you!

68
00:06:10,960 --> 00:06:11,790
Paralysis.

69
00:06:15,300 --> 00:06:16,130
Kittito!

70
00:06:23,040 --> 00:06:24,640
What's the plan now, huh?

71
00:06:24,960 --> 00:06:27,857
You gonna kill everyone here
and cover it up or something?

72
00:06:27,940 --> 00:06:28,920
Oh, God, no.

73
00:06:29,240 --> 00:06:31,917
That wouldn't be sporting
of me, now would it?

74
00:06:32,000 --> 00:06:33,760
No, I have a better idea.

75
00:06:34,320 --> 00:06:37,497
I'm going to head for the top floor
and wait for all of you there.

76
00:06:37,580 --> 00:06:39,404
I'll be inside the Ruby Palace.

77
00:06:39,780 --> 00:06:42,257
It's a shame I have to
leave you all so soon.

78
00:06:42,340 --> 00:06:44,357
I've spent lots of time
developing the Knights

79
00:06:44,440 --> 00:06:46,577
of the Blood Oath and other elite players.

80
00:06:46,660 --> 00:06:47,490
Oh well.

81
00:06:48,160 --> 00:06:51,631
You're all strong, so I'm sure
you'll reach me, eventually.

82
00:06:52,380 --> 00:06:54,240
But before I go...

83
00:06:55,820 --> 00:06:59,877
Kirito, I feel you deserve some kind
of reward for discovering my identity,

84
00:06:59,960 --> 00:07:02,140
so I'll give you a chance.

85
00:07:02,360 --> 00:07:03,320
Chance for what?

86
00:07:03,600 --> 00:07:06,420
To fight me one-on-one,
right here, right now.

87
00:07:06,900 --> 00:07:09,540
Oh, and my immortality
will be deactivated.

88
00:07:10,740 --> 00:07:12,437
Defeat me and you clear the game,

89
00:07:12,520 --> 00:07:15,177
and all of the players will be
able to log out from this world.

90
00:07:15,260 --> 00:07:16,436
No strings attached.

91
00:07:16,820 --> 00:07:17,800
What do you say?

92
00:07:19,380 --> 00:07:20,560
Don't do it, Kirito.

93
00:07:20,860 --> 00:07:21,920
I don't like it.

94
00:07:22,100 --> 00:07:23,276
We should fall back.

95
00:07:53,320 --> 00:07:54,580
I have to.

96
00:07:56,300 --> 00:07:58,657
Okay then, let's finish it.

97
00:07:58,740 --> 00:07:59,700
Kirito!

98
00:08:00,740 --> 00:08:01,570
I'm sorry.

99
00:08:01,653 --> 00:08:04,052
I can't run away if it means ending this.

100
00:08:04,840 --> 00:08:06,500
You better not die.

101
00:08:06,740 --> 00:08:07,680
You hear me?

102
00:08:08,740 --> 00:08:09,570
No.

103
00:08:09,653 --> 00:08:10,483
I'm gonna win.

104
00:08:10,740 --> 00:08:14,080
I promise I'm gonna end this world. Okay.

105
00:08:14,540 --> 00:08:16,800
I believe in you, Kirito.

106
00:08:28,180 --> 00:08:30,400
Kirito! Don't! Kirito!

107
00:08:33,440 --> 00:08:34,270
Egil.

108
00:08:35,740 --> 00:08:39,505
Thanks for supporting all the
players in the game since day one.

109
00:08:40,240 --> 00:08:41,180
Yeah, I knew.

110
00:08:41,460 --> 00:08:43,177
You act like you're all about the money,

111
00:08:43,260 --> 00:08:45,457
but I know you spent
every penny you had on

112
00:08:45,540 --> 00:08:48,011
helping the intermediate players level up.

113
00:08:49,660 --> 00:08:50,490
Klein?

114
00:08:52,300 --> 00:08:54,500
I'm sorry I bailed on you that day.

115
00:08:55,660 --> 00:08:57,520
I think about it all the time.

116
00:08:59,380 --> 00:09:00,420
Dammit, Kittito!

117
00:09:01,100 --> 00:09:02,276
Don't you apologize!

118
00:09:02,860 --> 00:09:04,700
Don't you dare apologize now!

119
00:09:05,020 --> 00:09:06,500
I won't accept it!

120
00:09:06,740 --> 00:09:10,977
I'll never accept it until we're on the
other side and you're buying me dinner,

121
00:09:11,060 --> 00:09:11,900
goddammit!

122
00:09:12,120 --> 00:09:13,060
You got it.

123
00:09:13,260 --> 00:09:15,060
See you on the other side.

124
00:09:22,360 --> 00:09:26,620
If it's okay, I have a final
request to make. What is it?

125
00:09:26,980 --> 00:09:29,100
I'm not planning on going down easy.

126
00:09:29,600 --> 00:09:31,140
So if I die today,

127
00:09:31,480 --> 00:09:36,020
I want your word that you'll fix
it so Asuna doesn't kill herself.

128
00:09:38,280 --> 00:09:39,460
As you wish.

129
00:09:40,100 --> 00:09:41,517
No, Kirito, that's not fair!

130
00:09:41,600 --> 00:09:44,660
You can't do that! It's not fair! No!

131
00:09:53,800 --> 00:09:54,630
Kiko!

132
00:09:55,740 --> 00:09:57,800
This isn't some in-game duel.

133
00:09:58,220 --> 00:10:00,020
It's a fight to the death.

134
00:10:00,940 --> 00:10:02,720
That's fine with me.

135
00:10:03,540 --> 00:10:05,380
Cause I'm gonna kill him!

136
00:10:14,640 --> 00:10:17,397
He can block whatever
I throw at him because

137
00:10:17,480 --> 00:10:20,600
he designed the dual
wielding skill and he knows

138
00:10:22,080 --> 00:10:22,962
all its combos.

139
00:10:23,300 --> 00:10:28,260
I have to beat him with my own power
without using the sword skills. Faster.

140
00:10:29,260 --> 00:10:30,780
I gotta go faster!

141
00:11:02,120 --> 00:11:04,000
I'm sorry, Asuna.

142
00:11:04,460 --> 00:11:06,660
Please, keep living.

143
00:11:17,500 --> 00:11:19,600
Game over, Kirito.

144
00:11:44,800 --> 00:11:49,540
Asuna, Asuna, you can't, you can't be.

145
00:11:54,540 --> 00:11:55,980
I'm sorry.

146
00:11:58,120 --> 00:11:59,100
Goodbye.

147
00:12:19,920 --> 00:12:21,440
Now that was a surprise.

148
00:12:21,860 --> 00:12:26,497
I'm sure I never programmed a way for
players to neutralize their own paralysis.

149
00:12:26,580 --> 00:12:29,109
I guess sometimes these
things just happen.

150
00:12:36,580 --> 00:12:37,410
Hmm?

151
00:12:50,660 --> 00:12:52,460
I don't know.

152
00:13:20,520 --> 00:13:22,640
It's over now.

153
00:13:26,740 --> 00:13:29,340
I believe in you, Kirito.

154
00:13:44,600 --> 00:13:46,377
Not yet.

155
00:13:46,460 --> 00:13:48,197
Not

156
00:13:48,280 --> 00:13:55,280
yet.

157
00:14:18,680 --> 00:14:21,820
We did it, didn't we?

158
00:14:56,300 --> 00:15:01,300
On November 7th at 2.55pm,
the game has been cleared.

159
00:15:01,740 --> 00:15:04,260
Repeat, the game has been cleared.

160
00:15:20,340 --> 00:15:22,280
Where am I?

161
00:15:33,520 --> 00:15:34,920
Kirito!

162
00:15:50,280 --> 00:15:51,400
I'm sorry.

163
00:15:51,760 --> 00:15:53,760
I guess I ended up dying too.

164
00:15:54,680 --> 00:15:55,510
Dummy.

165
00:16:11,240 --> 00:16:12,480
Where are we?

166
00:16:12,940 --> 00:16:14,000
Do you know?

167
00:16:28,680 --> 00:16:30,520
A stunning view, isn't it?

168
00:16:42,620 --> 00:16:44,100
At Argus headquarters,

169
00:16:44,580 --> 00:16:48,227
the SAO mainframe is in a room
five floors below street level,

170
00:16:48,400 --> 00:16:51,753
and right now it's deleting
all the data from its drives.

171
00:16:52,800 --> 00:16:57,180
In about ten minutes, everything in
this world will disappear forever.

172
00:16:58,580 --> 00:16:59,820
And all the players?

173
00:17:00,180 --> 00:17:01,440
What happens to them?

174
00:17:02,600 --> 00:17:04,659
You don't have to worry about them.

175
00:17:04,920 --> 00:17:11,440
The 6,147 players who survived the game up
to now were logged out a few seconds ago.

176
00:17:12,920 --> 00:17:15,880
And what about the 4,000 people who died?

177
00:17:16,320 --> 00:17:17,560
What about them?

178
00:17:18,760 --> 00:17:20,060
They'll never return.

179
00:17:20,520 --> 00:17:24,660
In any world, real or virtual,
once you're dead, you're gone.

180
00:17:28,580 --> 00:17:29,410
Why?

181
00:17:29,493 --> 00:17:30,323
What's the point?

182
00:17:30,560 --> 00:17:31,780
Why did you do this?

183
00:17:32,120 --> 00:17:33,840
That's a good question.

184
00:17:34,920 --> 00:17:37,508
It's been so long I've
forgotten the reason.

185
00:17:38,460 --> 00:17:39,660
Isn't that strange?

186
00:17:40,740 --> 00:17:45,564
Even before I developed a system for the
full-dive environment, I dreamed of this.

187
00:17:45,920 --> 00:17:50,360
A castle in a world that wasn't governed
by earthly laws and restrictions.

188
00:17:51,000 --> 00:17:53,941
I poured my life into
making that world a reality.

189
00:17:56,160 --> 00:17:57,737
I created this world,

190
00:17:57,820 --> 00:18:02,526
and I got to see something that surpassed
anything I could have imagined for it.

191
00:18:04,920 --> 00:18:07,557
My steel castle floating in the sky,

192
00:18:07,640 --> 00:18:10,997
I don't remember how old I was
when I became obsessed with it.

193
00:18:11,080 --> 00:18:15,617
I wanted to leave the earth
to fly to that castle;

194
00:18:15,700 --> 00:18:18,380
I wanted that more than anything else.

195
00:18:18,940 --> 00:18:20,720
For as long as I can remember.

196
00:18:24,940 --> 00:18:26,377
You know what, Kirito?

197
00:18:26,460 --> 00:18:29,197
I want to believe it's still out there.

198
00:18:29,280 --> 00:18:33,737
That somewhere in some other
world, my castle is still standing.

199
00:18:33,820 --> 00:18:34,880
taller than ever.

200
00:18:36,400 --> 00:18:37,230
Yeah.

201
00:18:37,900 --> 00:18:39,560
Maybe it still is.

202
00:18:45,740 --> 00:18:47,120
Before I forget,

203
00:18:47,740 --> 00:18:49,857
congratulations on clearing the game.

204
00:18:49,940 --> 00:18:51,740
Girito, Asuna.

205
00:18:55,500 --> 00:18:58,860
Well then, I should
probably get going now.

206
00:19:18,180 --> 00:19:19,640
I guess this is goodbye.

207
00:19:21,200 --> 00:19:22,840
This isn't goodbye at all.

208
00:19:23,640 --> 00:19:26,758
We're going to be together
when we finally disappear.

209
00:19:26,880 --> 00:19:29,115
So we're going to be together forever.

210
00:19:29,700 --> 00:19:32,340
Hey, you never told me your real name.

211
00:19:32,600 --> 00:19:34,835
Would you please tell me before we go?

212
00:19:38,440 --> 00:19:39,270
Kazuto.

213
00:19:39,353 --> 00:19:40,620
Kazuto Kirigaya.

214
00:19:40,960 --> 00:19:43,180
And last month I turned 16.

215
00:19:45,780 --> 00:19:47,177
Kazuto Kirigaya.

216
00:19:47,260 --> 00:19:49,180
So you're younger than me, huh?

217
00:19:49,940 --> 00:19:52,760
My name is Asuna Yuki.

218
00:19:53,220 --> 00:19:54,540
I'm 17 now.

219
00:19:56,100 --> 00:19:57,757
Asuna Yuki.

220
00:19:57,840 --> 00:19:59,080
Asuna Yuki.

221
00:20:06,920 --> 00:20:08,460
Sorry. Sorry.

222
00:20:08,880 --> 00:20:10,040
I swore.

223
00:20:10,440 --> 00:20:11,940
I promised I'd save you.

224
00:20:12,320 --> 00:20:14,160
Get you back to the real world.

225
00:20:14,380 --> 00:20:15,537
But I...

226
00:20:15,620 --> 00:20:17,380
I couldn't.

227
00:20:20,780 --> 00:20:21,620
It's okay.

228
00:20:22,880 --> 00:20:23,780
It's okay.

229
00:20:24,780 --> 00:20:26,877
I'm happy I got to meet you, Kazuto.

230
00:20:26,960 --> 00:20:28,357
And to be with you.

231
00:20:28,440 --> 00:20:29,940
And to live with you.

232
00:20:30,420 --> 00:20:33,538
This is the happiest I've
ever been in my whole life.

233
00:20:33,940 --> 00:20:35,260
Thank you for that.

234
00:20:35,800 --> 00:20:37,060
And I love you.

235
00:20:56,480 --> 00:21:00,240
I love you so very much.

236
00:21:29,860 --> 00:21:33,080
Oh, my God.

237
00:22:03,200 --> 00:22:04,600
Asuna.

238
00:22:14,460 --> 00:22:15,860
Asuna.

239
00:22:17,540 --> 00:22:22,337
I can hear the sound of the

240
00:22:22,420 --> 00:22:29,317
wind that is a little sad to me.

241
00:22:29,400 --> 00:22:33,380
But I will be stronger and stronger.

242
00:22:35,020 --> 00:22:36,902
I will be stronger and stronger.

243
00:22:58,180 --> 00:22:59,217
Thank you

244
00:22:59,300 --> 00:23:05,777
so

245
00:23:05,860 --> 00:23:06,690
much for watching.

246
00:23:06,773 --> 00:23:12,680
This is the world of no
wonder, even if it's a dream.

247
00:23:15,420 --> 00:23:18,720
Even if it's a dream, it's a dream.

248
00:23:19,680 --> 00:23:25,060
It's a dream, it's a dream.

249
00:23:27,200 --> 00:23:33,040
It's a dream, it's a dream.

250
00:23:35,800 --> 00:23:38,100
Next time, return.
